renderer: the museum's wallhack, for recordings only

r_demo_xray: before the normal draw, a player is drawn with the depth test
reversed and no texture — a faint orange tint where a wall hides them,
marked in the stencil, then the same part a little fatter where the mark
is not, which is an orange outline round a ghost. What is in plain sight
is drawn over it as usual, so hidden and seen cannot be confused. The
OpenGL wrapper wallhacks of 2000-2004 made visible, the "chams" of the
years after. Nothing outside a recording, whatever the cvar says; and only
the players the server sent, which was the anti-wallhack of its day. It
sits in R_StudioDrawPoints because that is where every path draws: the
Counter-Strike client has a studio renderer of its own and calls back into
the engine only to emit the triangles, so a switch in the engine's own
player routine (the first try) was never reached.

